    "prompt": "Function `_entries_from_toctree` in sphinx/environment/adapters/toctree.py. The statements below were written about this exact version of the function.\n\nFunction source (docstring removed):\n```python\ndef _entries_from_toctree(\n    env: BuildEnvironment,\n    prune: bool,\n    titles_only: bool,\n    collapse: bool,\n    includehidden: bool,\n    tags: Tags,\n    toctree_ancestors: Set[str],\n    included: Matcher,\n    excluded: Matcher,\n    toctreenode: addnodes.toctree,\n    parents: list[str],\n    subtree: bool = False,\n) -> list[Element]:\n    entries: list[Element] = []\n    for title, ref in toctreenode['entries']:\n        try:\n            toc, refdoc = _toctree_entry(\n                title,\n                ref,\n                env,\n                prune,\n                collapse,\n                tags,\n                toctree_ancestors,\n                included,\n                excluded,\n                toctreenode,\n                parents,\n            )\n        except LookupError:\n            continue\n\n        # children of toc are:\n        # - list_item + compact_paragraph + (reference and subtoc)\n        # - only + subtoc\n        # - toctree\n        children: Iterable[nodes.Element] = toc.children  # type: ignore[assignment]\n\n        # if titles_only is given, only keep the main title and\n        # sub-toctrees\n        if titles_only:\n            # delete everything but the toplevel title(s)\n            # and toctrees\n            for top_level in children:\n                # nodes with length 1 don't have any children anyway\n                if len(top_level) > 1:\n                    if subtrees := list(top_level.findall(addnodes.toctree)):\n                        top_level[1][:] = subtrees  # type: ignore[index]\n                    else:\n                        top_level.pop(1)\n        # resolve all sub-toctrees\n        for sub_toc_node in list(toc.findall(addnodes.toctree)):\n            if sub_toc_node.get('hidden', False) and not includehidden:\n                continue\n            for i, entry in enumerate(\n                _entries_from_toctree(\n                    env,\n                    prune,\n                    titles_only,\n                    collapse,\n                    includehidden,\n                    tags,\n                    toctree_ancestors,\n                    included,\n                    excluded,\n                    sub_toc_node,\n                    [refdoc, *parents],\n                    subtree=True,\n                ),\n                start=sub_toc_node.parent.index(sub_toc_node) + 1,\n            ):\n                sub_toc_node.parent.insert(i, entry)\n            sub_toc_node.parent.remove(sub_toc_node)\n\n        entries.extend(children)\n\n    if not subtree:\n        ret = nodes.bullet_list()\n        ret += entries\n        return [ret]\n\n    return entries\n```\n\nFacts extracted from this version by a parser (tree-sitter):\nsignature: _entries_from_toctree(env, prune, titles_only, collapse, includehidden, tags, toctree_ancestors, included, excluded, toctreenode, parents, subtree) -> list[Element]\ncalls: _entries_from_toctree, _toctree_entry, entries.extend, enumerate, len, list, nodes.bullet_list, sub_toc_node.get, sub_toc_node.parent.index, sub_toc_node.parent.insert, sub_toc_node.parent.remove, toc.findall, top_level.findall, top_level.pop\nreturn statements: return [ret] | return entries\nraise statements: (none)\ncontrol flow: if=5 loops=4 try=1 with=0 returns=2 yields=0 awaits=0\n\n\nStatements:\nS1. _entries_from_toctree extracts table of contents (TOC) entries from a `toctree` node in the document structure.\nS2. _entries_from_toctree is a core component of Sphinx's documentation generation process.\nS3. _entries_from_toctree accepts a set of tags.\nS4. _entries_from_toctree filters content based on various criteria like pruning, collapsing, and tag inclusion.\nS5. _entries_from_toctree accepts a list 